   <define name="gameplayTrope">
      <element name="gameplayTrope">
         <a:documentation xmlns:a="http://relaxng.org/ns/compatibility/annotations/1.0">(Gameplay Trope) A generally recognizable [gameplay] device or convention [appearing in the footage]. [Gameplay] tropes rely on culturally mediated expectations to expedite the development of [mechanics, action, agency, experiences, and] events. When overused or oversimplified, tropes often come at the expense of fair and inclusive representations (Lee et al., VGMS 4.2, 2024)This element will typically be repeated.See TV Tropes for definitions and examples of most tropes in this controlled vocabulary. The use of TV Tropes should be accompanied by peer-reviewed scholarship in Media and Game Studies.Controlled vocabulary adapted, with changes and additions, from Lee et al., "Controlled Vocabulary for Tropes," 2024, and TV Tropes 2026.</a:documentation>
         <choice>
            <value>Action commands</value>
            <a:documentation xmlns:a="http://relaxng.org/ns/compatibility/annotations/1.0"/>
